		<div style="display: contents"><!--[--><!--[--><!----><!--[--><!----><div class="gradio-container gradio-container-6-12-0 svelte-99kmwu" data-iframe-height="" style="min-height: initial; flex-grow: 1;"><!--[!--><!--]--> <div class="main fillable svelte-99kmwu app"><!--[--><!--[!--><!--[--><div class="wrap svelte-zxu34v" style="min-height: 100%;"><main class="contain svelte-zxu34v" style="flex-grow: 1; margin-right: 0;"><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!----><div id="" class="column  svelte-siq5d6" style="min-width: calc(min(0px, 100%));"><!--[!--><!--]--> <!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!----><!--[--><!----><div id="" class="block  svelte-1plpy97 padded hide-container auto-margin" dir="ltr" style="--start-top: 0px; --start-left: 0px; --start-width: 0px; --start-height: 0px; border-style: solid; overflow: auto; min-width: calc(min(0px, 100%));"><!--[--><div class="wrap center full svelte-1uj8rng hide" data-testid="status-tracker" style="position: absolute; padding: 0;"><!--[!--><!--]--> <!--[!--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--]--></div> <!--[!--><!--]--><!----> <div class="svelte-16ln60g"><div class="prose  svelte-1xjkzpp" data-testid="markdown" dir="ltr"><!--[!--><!--]--> <span class="md svelte-1hf8a14 prose"><!----><h1>See-through: Single-image Layer Decomposition for Anime Characters</h1>
<p><a href="https://github.com/shitagaki-lab/see-through" target="_blank">GitHub</a> | <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.03749" target="_blank">Paper (arXiv:2602.03749)</a></p>
<p>Upload an anime character illustration to decompose it into fully-inpainted semantic layers with depth ordering, exported as a layered PSD file.</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> 768 resolution is recommended for ZeroGPU free tier. Higher resolutions may timeout or exhaust your daily quota. For best quality, clone the <a href="https://github.com/shitagaki-lab/see-through" target="_blank">full repo</a> and run <code>inference_psd.py</code> locally. We also have a <a href="https://github.com/jtydhr88/ComfyUI-See-through" target="_blank">ComfyUI Node Extension</a> and other community extensions — check our repo for more details.</p>
<p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This demo uses a newer model checkpoint and may not fully reproduce identical results reported in the paper.</p>
